  abstract = {How can we audit an AI system before it is safe or practical to deploy? This question is difficult because historical operational logs, generated by a behavior policy, may fail to cover the states visited by the target policy. We study this problem by proposing a hybrid auditing framework that combines fixed operational logs, generated by a behavior policy, with a small number of actively collected audit trials. We formulate probe design as a constrained convex optimization problem that minimizes the mismatch between the combined sampling distribution and the distribution induced by the target policy. The resulting probe allocates trials toward audit blind spots, namely regions frequently visited by the target policy but poorly covered by operational logs. Then, we develop an iterative algorithm that estimates the environment dynamics and distribution induced by the target policy from data while refining the probe design. Theoretically, we prove that minimizing this mismatch bounds the estimator's mean squared error and asymptotic variance. Experiments on GridWorld and LunarLander environments show that the proposed method substantially outperforms baseline methods.},
